<article class="env-lemma" id="092E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/092E">Lemma <span data-tag="092E">15.106.4</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a weakly étale ring map. If $A$ has weak dimension at most $d$, then so does $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $N$ be a $B$-module. If $d = 0$, then $N$ is flat as an $A$-module, hence flat as a $B$-module by Lemma <a href="/tag/092C" data-tag="092C">15.106.2</a>. Assume $d > 0$. Choose a resolution $F_\bullet \to N$ by free $B$-modules. Our assumption implies that $K = \mathop{\mathrm{Im}}(F_ d \to F_{d - 1})$ is $A$-flat, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0653" data-tag="0653">15.68.2</a>. Hence it is $B$-flat by Lemma <a href="/tag/092C" data-tag="092C">15.106.2</a>. Thus $0 \to K \to F_{d - 1} \to \ldots \to F_0 \to N \to 0$ is a flat resolution of length $d$ and we see that $N$ has tor dimension at most $d$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>